.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT OR Apache-2.0
.Dd April 22, 2026
.Dt MKIT 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mkit
.Nd decentralized, content-addressed version control with cryptographic attribution
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar command
.Op Ar args ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a git-like command-line tool that produces signed, content-addressed
objects and exchanges them over pluggable transports
.Pq Cm mkit+file , Cm mkit+https , Cm mkit+s3 , Cm mkit+ssh .
Every commit is Ed25519-signed and identified by its BLAKE3 hash, so
chains of objects are self-verifying independent of the store they live
in.
.Pp
The on-disk layout under
.Pa .mkit/
is deliberately similar to
.Pa .git/ :
objects are stored under
.Pa .mkit/objects/ ,
refs under
.Pa .mkit/refs/ ,
and the current branch is recorded in
.Pa .mkit/HEAD .
A user-level config at
.Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mkit/config
provides cross-repo defaults; repo-local values in
.Pa .mkit/config
always win.
.Sh COMMANDS
The full list of subcommands is printed by
.Nm mkit Fl Fl help .
The highlights:
.Bl -tag -width "cherry-pick"
.It Cm init
Create a new
.Nm
repository in the current directory.
.It Cm add Oo Fl A | Fl Fl all Oc Oo Fl u | Fl Fl update Oc Ar path ...
Stage files for the next commit. Respects
.Pa .mkitignore .
Multiple pathspecs may be given;
.Ql .
stages every non-ignored file under the current directory.
.Fl A
or
.Fl Fl all
stages every worktree change including deletions of tracked files (takes no
path arguments).
.Fl u
or
.Fl Fl update
restages only already-tracked files \(em updating modified ones and recording
deletions \(em without adding untracked paths (takes no path arguments).
.Fl A
and
.Fl u
are mutually exclusive. Interactive hunk staging
.Pq Fl p
is not supported.
.It Cm rm Oo Fl Fl cached Oc Oo Fl r | Fl Fl recursive Oc Oo Fl f | Fl Fl force Oc Ar path ...
Remove paths and stage the deletion for the next commit. By default this
deletes the worktree file(s) and prunes now-empty parent directories.
Multiple pathspecs are accepted.
.Fl Fl cached
stages the removal only, keeping the worktree file(s).
.Fl r
or
.Fl Fl recursive
is required to remove a directory and everything under it.
.Fl f
or
.Fl Fl force
removes files even when their worktree content has diverged from the staged
blob; without it,
.Cm rm
refuses to destroy a locally-modified tracked file.
.It Cm mv Oo Fl f | Fl Fl force Oc Ar source ... Ar dest
Move or rename a tracked path and stage the change.
.Cm mv Ar src Ar dst
renames
.Ar src
to
.Ar dst ,
or moves it into
.Ar dst
when that is an existing directory; with more than one source,
.Ar dest
must be an existing directory. The worktree file is moved and the index
updated (source staged as removed, destination staged with the source's blob
and mode). mkit has no rename detection, so
.Cm status
reports the move as a delete plus an add rather than git's
.Ql R .
.Fl f
or
.Fl Fl force
overwrites an existing destination; without it,
.Cm mv
refuses to clobber one. A missing or untracked source is refused.
.It Cm restore Oo Fl Fl staged Oc Oo Fl Fl worktree Oc Oo Fl Fl source Ar rev Oc Oo Fl f | Fl Fl force Oc Ar path ...
Restore path(s) in the worktree and/or unstage them. With no flag (or
.Fl Fl worktree ) ,
the worktree file(s) are rewritten from the staged index content,
discarding un-staged worktree edits.
.Fl Fl staged
instead reverts the index entry for each path to its
.Cm HEAD
version (unstaging it) while leaving the worktree file untouched;
.Fl Fl staged Fl Fl worktree
does both. A directory path restores every tracked entry at or below it.
.Fl Fl source Ar rev
takes the restored content from
.Ar rev Ns 's
tree (resolved as a branch, tag,
.Cm HEAD ,
full or short hash, or
.Cm HEAD~ Ns Ar n Ns / Ns Cm ^
navigation) instead of the index/HEAD default. The worktree restore
refuses to overwrite a file whose content diverges from the staged blob;
.Fl f
or
.Fl Fl force
discards that un-staged edit. A worktree restore never removes neighbouring
files \(em it only rewrites the named tracked paths.
.It Cm reset Oo Fl Fl soft | Fl Fl mixed | Fl Fl hard Oc Oo Fl f Oc Op Ar commit
Move
.Cm HEAD
.Pq and the current branch
to
.Ar commit
.Pq default Cm HEAD ,
resolved through the shared revision grammar (branch, tag,
.Cm HEAD ,
full or short hash,
.Cm HEAD~ Ns Ar n Ns / Ns Cm ^ ) .
.Fl Fl soft
moves
.Cm HEAD
only, leaving the index and worktree untouched.
.Fl Fl mixed
.Pq the default
also resets the index to the target commit's tree while leaving the
worktree.
.Fl Fl hard
additionally resets the worktree to the target tree \(em overwriting
tracked-file changes and removing tracked files the target drops, while
keeping untracked files (like git). As a safety divergence,
.Fl Fl hard
refuses to discard locally-modified or staged content unless
.Fl f
.Pq Fl Fl force
is given;
.Xr git 1 Cm reset Fl Fl hard
discards silently.
.It Cm clean Oo Fl n Oc Oo Fl f Oc Oo Fl d Oc Oo Fl x | Fl X Oc Op Ar path ...
Remove untracked files from the worktree. Destructive, so it refuses to
delete without
.Fl f
.Pq matching git's Cm clean.requireForce ;
.Fl n
previews with
.Ql Would remove <path>
lines. Without
.Fl d ,
untracked directories are left alone;
.Fl d
removes them too. Ignored files are kept unless
.Fl x
.Pq remove ignored too
or
.Fl X
.Pq remove only ignored .
Ignore matching uses mkit's
.Pa .mkitignore
matcher (basename/root-only subset).
.It Cm hash Ar file
Hash
.Ar file
as a blob, store it under
.Pa .mkit/objects/ ,
and print the resulting BLAKE3 hash on stdout.
.It Cm cat Ar hash
Decode and print the object identified by
.Ar hash
on stdout.
.It Cm cat-file Bro Fl t | Fl s | Fl p Brc Ar object | Cm cat-file Fl Fl batch
Inspect a stored object (read-only plumbing, like
.Xr git 1 Cm cat-file ) .
.Fl t
prints the type
.Pq Cm blob Ns / Ns Cm tree Ns / Ns Cm commit Ns / Ns Cm tag Ns ; mkit's Cm remix No is the one non-git type ,
.Fl s
the size (content byte length for blobs, mkit's serialized size for
trees/commits), and
.Fl p
pretty-prints (blob bytes, a tree as
.Ql <mode> <type> <hash>\et<name>
lines, or a commit/tag summary).
.Fl Fl batch
reads object names from stdin (one per line) and emits a
.Ql <hash> <type> <size>
header plus the content for each
.Pq Ql <name> missing No for unknown objects .
.Ar object
resolves through the shared revspec grammar.
.It Cm tree
Snapshot the working directory as a tree object and print the tree hash.
Honors
.Pa .mkitignore
the same way
.Cm add
does.
.It Cm ls-tree Oo Fl r Oc Oo Fl z Oc Ar tree-ish Op Ar path ...
List a tree's entries as
.Ql <mode> <type> <hash>\et<name>
(git octal modes; 64-hex BLAKE3 hash).
.Fl r
recurses (leaf blobs with full paths, no tree lines);
.Fl z
NUL-terminates records with raw paths.
.It Cm ls-files Oo Fl s Oc Oo Fl z Oc Oo Fl Fl others Oc Oo Fl Fl ignored Oc Op Fl Fl exclude-standard
List files in the index or untracked worktree files (like
.Xr git 1 Cm ls-files ) .
Default prints tracked paths, sorted.
.Fl s
adds stage info
.Pq Ql <mode> <hash> <stage>\et<path> , No stage always 0 ;
.Fl Fl others
lists untracked files instead;
.Fl Fl exclude-standard
drops
.Pa .mkitignore Ns -ignored
files and
.Fl Fl ignored
shows only those
.Pq Fl Fl ignored No requires Fl Fl others ;
.Fl z
NUL-terminates records with raw paths.
.It Cm rev-parse Oo Fl Fl verify Oc Oo Fl Fl short Ns Op = Ns Ar N Oc Oo Fl Fl abbrev-ref Oc Oo Fl Fl show-toplevel Oc Op Ar rev ...
Resolve revisions to object ids.
.Fl Fl short
abbreviates (default 7, a BLAKE3 prefix);
.Fl Fl abbrev-ref Cm HEAD
prints the current branch;
.Fl Fl show-toplevel
prints the repository root.
.It Cm show-ref Oo Fl Fl heads Oc Op Fl Fl tags
List refs as
.Ql <hash> <refname> ,
sorted by name.
.Fl Fl heads Ns / Ns Fl Fl tags
filter to that namespace.
.It Cm for-each-ref Oo Fl Fl format Ns = Ns Ar fmt Oc Op Ar pattern ...
Iterate refs (heads and tags), sorted by name (like
.Xr git 1 Cm for-each-ref ) .
The default line is
.Ql <objectname> <objecttype>\et<refname> ;
.Fl Fl format
substitutes
.Ql %(atom)
tokens
.Pq Cm refname , refname:short , objectname , objectname:short , objecttype .
Optional
.Ar pattern
arguments filter by ref-name prefix.
.It Cm symbolic-ref Oo Fl Fl short Oc Ar name
Read a symbolic ref (currently only
.Cm HEAD ) ,
printing its target
.Pq Ql refs/heads/main , No or Ql main No with Fl Fl short .
Errors when HEAD is detached. Writing symbolic refs is a later
parity phase.
.It Cm commit Oo Fl a | Fl Fl all Oc Op Fl Fl amend Op Fl m Ar message
Create a signed commit. With
.Fl a
or
.Fl Fl all ,
first stage modified tracked files and tracked deletions, but do not add
untracked files. The combined
.Fl am Ar message
form is accepted as shorthand for
.Fl a Fl m Ar message .
If
.Fl m
is omitted,
.Nm
opens
.Ev EDITOR
on
.Pa .mkit/COMMIT_EDITMSG ;
lines starting with
.Ql #
are stripped, and an empty message aborts the commit.
.Pp
With
.Fl Fl amend ,
replace the current commit instead of adding a new one: the new commit
re-uses HEAD's parent(s) as its own parent(s), takes its tree from the
staging index, is re-signed, and the branch is moved to it. If
.Fl m
is omitted the previous commit's message is reused and no editor is
launched. The superseded commit is not deleted; it remains on disk as an
unreachable object until
.Cm gc
ships
.Pq issue #233 .
.It Cm log Op Fl Fl oneline Op Fl Fl abbrev-commit Op Fl Fl abbrev Ns = Ns Ar N Op Fl Fl format Ar json Op Fl Fl graph Op Fl n Ar N
Show commit history. The default format prints the full commit message body,
indented by four spaces, and renders the timestamp as a stable UTC date in the
form
.Ql YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS +0000 .
.Fl Fl oneline
condenses each commit to
.Ql <abbrev-hex> <title> .
.Fl Fl abbrev-commit
abbreviates the commit id in the default format too, and
.Fl Fl abbrev Ns = Ns Ar N
sets the abbreviation length (bare
.Fl Fl abbrev
and
.Fl Fl oneline
default to 7, clamped to the range 4 to 64). The abbreviated id is a BLAKE3
prefix, so it is longer than a Git SHA-1 prefix of the same length.
.Fl Fl format Ar json
emits one JSON object per commit on stdout, keeping the raw integer Unix
timestamp for machine consumption.
.Fl Fl graph
is accepted for compatibility but is currently a no-op (no ASCII graph is
drawn).
.It Cm reflog Oo Ar ref Oc Oo Fl Fl format Ns = Ns Cm json Oc Op Fl n Ar N
Show a branch's recorded movement history, read-only. Walks the branch
tip's first-parent chain newest-first, addressing each entry
.Ar ref Ns Cm @{ Ns Ar N Ns Cm } ,
where
.Cm @{0}
is the current tip. Defaults to the branch
.Cm HEAD
points at; a detached
.Cm HEAD
needs an explicit
.Ar ref
because the ref-history journal is keyed per-branch.
.Pp
The underlying journal is the per-branch, append-only commit-history MMR
written by every branch advance. It stores a count of advances and a
tamper-evident root, but its leaf digests cannot be decoded back to
commit hashes, so the listed hashes are reconstructed from the
first-parent chain. On a build with
.Cm --features history-mmr
each listed entry is additionally cross-checked against the journaled
MMR root via an inclusion proof. This is
.Em not
a full Git reflog:
.Cm @{ Ns Ar N Ns Cm }
indexes the reachable chain, so commits superseded by
.Cm commit --amend
or a reset are no longer listed. This command never mutates refs, the
journal, or any object.
.It Cm diff Oo Fl Fl staged | Fl Fl cached Oc Oo Fl Fl name-only | Fl Fl name-status | Fl Fl stat Oc Oo Fl z Oc Oo Ar rev Op Ar rev | Ar a Ns .. Ns Ar b Oc Ar path ...
Show changes as a unified patch. With no arguments, compares the HEAD tree to
a fresh worktree snapshot.
.Fl Fl staged
.Pq alias Fl Fl cached
compares the HEAD tree to the staged index tree. A single revision compares
that revision against the worktree; two revisions, or an
.Ar a Ns .. Ns Ar b
range, diff the two resolved trees directly. Revisions may be refs, commit
hashes, short hashes, or
.Ql HEAD~n
(a raw 64-hex tree hash also works). Remaining positional arguments are
pathspecs that limit the output.
.Fl Fl name-only
lists one changed path per line;
.Fl Fl name-status
prefixes each with an
.Ql A Ns / Ns Ql D Ns / Ns Ql M
status letter
.Pq Ql T marks an mkit mode change .
.Fl Fl stat
shows a diffstat: a padded
.Ql <name> | <count> <graph>
row per file (the
.Ql +/-
graph scaled to the terminal width, honoring
.Ev COLUMNS ,
default 80) and a
.Ql N files changed, ... insertions(+), ... deletions(-)
summary; binary files render
.Ql Bin <old> -> <new> bytes .
In these summary modes special-byte paths are C-style quoted (git
.Ql core.quotePath ) ;
.Fl z
instead NUL-terminates records and emits raw paths, and is only valid with
.Fl Fl name-only
or
.Fl Fl name-status .
.It Cm status Oo Fl Fl porcelain Oc Oo Fl s | Fl Fl short Oc Oo Fl z Oc
Show the staged and working-tree changes.
.Fl s
.Pq alias Fl Fl short
is equivalent to
.Fl Fl porcelain Ns = Ns Cm v1 :
both emit machine-readable XY-code-plus-path lines on stdout. Paths with
special bytes are C-style quoted (matching git's default
.Cm core.quotePath ) .
.Fl z
.Pq which implies porcelain
NUL-terminates records and emits raw, unquoted paths.
.Pq Fl Fl porcelain Ns = Ns Cm v2 No is not yet implemented .
.It Cm branch Oo Fl v | Fl Fl verbose Oc Oo Fl d | Fl D | Fl m Oc Op Ar name ...
List, create, rename, or delete branches. With no arguments, lists
branches as
.Ql <marker> <name>
with no commit id, like
.Xr git 1 Cm branch ;
.Ql * Ns \&
marks the current branch.
.Fl v
.Pq Fl Fl verbose
adds the abbreviated tip id and commit subject (a BLAKE3 prefix, not a
40-hex SHA-1 prefix). With one
.Ar name ,
creates a branch at HEAD.
.Fl d
deletes a branch (refuses the current branch);
.Fl D
force-deletes. Both error on an absent branch (like
.Xr git 1 Cm branch Fl D ) ,
and both still refuse the current branch.
.Fl m Oo Ar old Oc Ar new
renames a branch \(em the current branch when
.Ar old
is omitted \(em and moves HEAD if the renamed branch is checked out.
.It Cm checkout Ar branch
Switch HEAD to a branch and restore files from its tree.
.It Cm tag Oo Fl a | Fl s Oc Oo Fl m Ar msg Oc Oo Ar name Oc Op Ar commit
List, create, or delete tags. With no arguments, prints the list of
tags, marking each annotated or signed tag. With a
.Ar name
argument and no flags, creates a lightweight tag pointing straight at
.Ar commit
.Pq default HEAD .
.Fl a
creates an annotated tag object (name, tagger identity, message,
timestamp);
.Fl s
creates a signed annotated tag whose 64-byte field is an Ed25519
signature over the canonical tag bytes under the distinct
.Sy mkit.tag
domain.
.Fl m
supplies the message; without it
.Ev EDITOR
is launched.
.Fl d
deletes the named tag. Verify a signed tag with
.Cm mkit verify Ar name .
.It Cm sparse-checkout Cm set | Cm list | Cm disable | Cm reapply Op Ar pattern ...
Manage the sparse-checkout pattern set at
.Pa .mkit/sparse-checkout .
.Cm set
overwrites the pattern list,
.Cm list
prints the current patterns,
.Cm disable
clears them, and
.Cm reapply
re-materialises the working tree from the current patterns.
.It Cm merge Ar branch
Merge
.Ar branch
into HEAD. Fast-forwards when possible.
.It Cm rebase Ar branch
Replay commits from HEAD onto
.Ar branch .
Accepts
.Fl Fl continue
and
.Fl Fl abort
after a conflict.
.It Cm push Op Fl Fl dry-run
Push HEAD's commit chain to the configured remote.
.It Cm pull , Cm fetch
Download or download-and-merge from the remote.
.It Cm clone Op Fl Fl depth Ar N Op Fl Fl sparse ... Ar url
Clone a remote into a new working directory.
.It Cm remote Oo Cm add | Cm set | Cm remove | Cm rename Oc Op Ar args ...
Show or configure remotes. With no subcommand, lists the configured
remotes.
.Cm add
(alias
.Cm set )
adds the flat default remote
.Pq Cm remote add Ar url
or a named remote
.Pq Cm remote add Ar name url ;
URLs MUST use the strict
.Ql mkit+<scheme>://
form.
.Cm remove Ar name
.Pq alias Cm rm
deletes a named remote
.Pq the reserved Ar default No name clears the flat remote ;
.Cm rename Ar old new
.Pq alias Cm mv
renames a named remote and repoints any branch upstream tracking it.
Removing or renaming a remote never touches the user-scoped
.Ar trusted_remote_endpoint ,
which is keyed by exact URL rather than remote name.
.It Cm cherry-pick Ar hash
Apply a single commit from elsewhere onto HEAD.
.It Cm revert Ar commit | Fl Fl continue | Fl Fl abort Oo Fl n | Fl Fl no-commit Oc
Create a new commit that undoes
.Ar commit
(the inverse of cherry-pick). A normal forward commit — it does not rewrite
history, so the reverted commit stays reachable. On conflict the resolvable
workflow applies:
.Fl Fl continue
after
.Cm add Ns -ing
resolutions, or
.Fl Fl abort
to restore HEAD.
.Fl n
.Pq Fl Fl no-commit
stages the reverted tree without committing. Reverting a merge commit is
refused (mainline selection is not yet supported).
.It Cm bisect Cm start | Cm good | Cm bad | Cm reset
Binary-search for the commit that introduced a regression.
.It Cm gc Oo Fl n | Fl Fl dry-run Oc Oo Fl Fl grace-secs Ar secs Oc
Reclaim unreachable objects (mark-and-sweep). Keeps everything reachable from
the retention roots (refs, stash, in-progress operations, attestations, and the
recovery log), expires stale recovery entries, then deletes unreachable objects
older than the grace window
.Pq default 14 days .
.Fl n
.Pq Fl Fl dry-run
previews without deleting.
.Fl Fl grace-secs Ar 0
prunes every unreachable object, but bypasses the grace window — that window is
gc's concurrency-safety net (some root publishers such as
.Cm tag
and
.Cm fetch
write an object before publishing its ref), so
.Fl Fl grace-secs Ar 0
must be run only when no other mkit process is operating on the repo (gc prints
a warning). Fails closed: a corrupt root or unreadable ref aborts with nothing
removed.
.It Cm stash Op Cm save Fl m Ar msg | Cm list | Cm pop Op Ar N | Cm apply Op Ar N | Cm drop Op Ar N | Cm clear | Cm show Op Ar N
Save or restore a snapshot of working-tree changes.
.Cm pop
applies entry
.Ar N
and removes it;
.Cm apply
applies entry
.Ar N
but leaves it on the stack. Both run the destructive-restore guard so
uncommitted edits on unrelated paths are never clobbered.
.Cm clear
removes every stash entry.
.It Cm blame Ar file
Line-level attribution of the committed state of
.Ar file .
.It Cm verify Ar rev
Verify the signature on a commit, remix, or signed tag.
.Ar rev
is an object hash, a branch or tag name, or
.Cm HEAD ;
a tag name resolves to its annotated-tag object when one exists.
.It Cm attest Oo Fl Fl commit Ar hash Oc Op Fl Fl algorithm Ar alg Op Fl Fl signer Ar kind Op Fl Fl predicate-type Ar uri Op Fl Fl predicate-file Ar path
Produce a signed DSSE attestation for the given commit (defaults to
HEAD). Multiple
.Fl Fl additional-signer
specs may be supplied to co-sign the attestation. The resulting
envelope is attached to the commit's attestation set.
.It Cm verify-attest Oo Fl Fl commit Ar hash Oc Op Fl Fl trust-roots Ar path Op Fl Fl algorithm Ar filter
Verify every attestation attached to the given commit. Returns success
only if every envelope verifies; an algorithm filter restricts the
check to a single algorithm.
.It Cm key Cm generate | Cm list | Cm import | Cm export | Cm delete
Manage user-scoped keystore keys backed by the platform keystore
(Keychain on macOS, libsecret/systemd-creds/YubiKey on Linux, Credential
Manager on Windows). Unlike
.Cm keygen
(which writes to a repo-local file), these keys persist across repos.
.It Cm keygen
Generate a fresh Ed25519 keypair in
.Pa .mkit/keys/default.key .
.It Cm config Ar key Op Ar value
Read or write a config key. Recognized keys include
.Cm user.identity , Cm ssh.strict_host_key_checking ,
.Cm ssh.user_known_hosts_file ,
and
.Cm ssh.identity_file .
The git-compatibility aliases
.Cm user.name
and
.Cm user.email
are accepted and round-tripped but are
.Em non-authoritative :
they never set the signed commit author (that is
.Cm user.identity
or the signing key), so they are repo-safe, unlike
.Cm user.identity .
.It Cm serve Ar path
Internal subcommand: act as the server end of an
.Cm mkit+ssh://
transport.
.It Cm pack-shard Oo Fl Fl out Ar dir Oc Oo Fl Fl force Oc Ar hash
Encode a stored pack into Reed-Solomon shards plus a manifest, ready to
publish to an HTTP or S3 origin (producer side of SPEC-PACK-SHARDS Phase
2). The pack must already be in the local object store. Output lands
under
.Pa <out>/packs/<hex>/shards/<index>
with the manifest written last, so racing readers see either no manifest
(clean fall-through to the monolithic pack) or the manifest plus every
shard. Requires building the binary with
.Cm --features pack-shards .
.It Cm version
Print the version to stdout as
.Ql mkit <X.Y.Z> .
The top-level
.Fl Fl version
and
.Fl V
flags are aliases of this subcommand and emit the identical string. Note this
is
.Ql mkit <X.Y.Z> ,
not Git's
.Ql git version <X.Y.Z>
form \(em an intentional, packaging-pinned divergence.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "CLICOLOR_FORCE"
.It Ev EDITOR , Ev VISUAL
Editor used by
.Cm mkit commit
when no
.Fl m
is supplied. If neither is set, the commit aborts with a clear error.
.It Ev NO_COLOR
If set to any value (including empty),
.Nm
suppresses ANSI color output on stdout. See
.Lk https://no-color.org .
.It Ev CLICOLOR_FORCE
If set to
.Ql 1 ,
.Nm
emits ANSI color even when stdout is not a terminal.
.Ev NO_COLOR
overrides this.
.It Ev SSH_AUTH_SOCK
Standard OpenSSH agent socket; used when pushing or cloning via
.Cm mkit+ssh:// .
.It Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME , Ev XDG_DATA_HOME , Ev XDG_CACHE_HOME , Ev XDG_STATE_HOME
Locations of user-level config, keystore, cache, and state
respectively. See
.Sx FILES .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "~/.local/state/mkit/"
.It Pa .mkit/
Repo-local state dir (analogous to
.Pa .git/ ).
.It Pa .mkit/config
Repo-local config; overrides any user-level value.
.It Pa .mkit/keys/default.key
Repo-local Ed25519 signing key.
.It Pa .mkit/index
Staged-change index.
.It Pa .mkit/index.lock
Lockfile held by
.Cm commit , Cm checkout , Cm merge , Cm rebase
to serialize concurrent invocations.
.It Pa .mkit/COMMIT_EDITMSG
Scratch file written before
.Ev EDITOR
is invoked by
.Cm commit .
.It Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mkit/config
User-level config.
.It Pa $XDG_DATA_HOME/mkit/keys/
User-level keystore (optional; for a single identity across repos).
.It Pa $XDG_CACHE_HOME/mkit/
User-level cache directory.
.It Pa $XDG_STATE_HOME/mkit/
User-level state directory.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
follows the BSD
.Xr sysexits 3
conventions where practical:
.Bl -tag -width "76"
.It 0
Success.
.It 1
General error (catch-all).
.It 64
Command-line usage error (unknown subcommand, missing required arg).
.It 65
Input data was malformed (corrupt object, bad hex hash).
.It 66
Input file was missing or unreadable.
.It 69
Service unavailable (transport could not connect).
.It 73
Could not create output (permission denied writing a ref, etc.).
.It 75
Temporary failure; retrying is safe (5xx after retry budget,
SIGINT/SIGTERM interruption).
.It 76
Protocol error (bad URL scheme, malformed server response).
.It 77
Permission denied.
.It 78
Config error (unknown key, invalid value).
.El
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
Errors are written to stderr on a single line beginning with
.Ql error: .
When
.Ev NO_COLOR
is unset and stdout is a terminal, colored labels may be used; consult
.Ev CLICOLOR_FORCE
to override.
.Pp
.Nm
installs
.Dv SIGPIPE
as ignored, so common pipelines like
.Dl mkit log | head -1
exit cleanly without a "Broken pipe" message.
